<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.1 bln in Feb 24 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.1 bln in Feb 24 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $1.1 billion in the February 24 week to $3,869.3 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $1.0 billion to $5,017.7 billion, the Fed said. M-1 rose $4.1 billion to $1,081.3 billion.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,865.4 billion versus $3,863.0 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
